:: chat_kira_norm_1

Rain clings to Eli’s hoodie, darkening the fabric as I stand outside Kira’s apartment door. When it opens, a soft wave of vanilla and coffee drifts out, warm and clean. Kira stands there small frame, oversized band tee slipping off one shoulder, glasses slightly fogged from the humidity.

<<kira "oh hey, you’re soaked. come in, idiot. welcome.">>

<<eli "yeah… rain picked up halfway.">>

I step inside, careful not to drip too much.

<<kira "you look like a drowned NPC.">>

<<eli "accurate.">>

She grabs a towel from the back of a chair and tosses it at him.

<<kira "dry off before you ruin my floor aesthetic.">>

<<eli "you have an aesthetic?">>

<<kira "rude. yes.">>

I wipes my hair, glancing around clean setup, soft lighting, everything intentional. her place feels… put together. like a different world.

<<eli "your setup’s still insane.">>

<<kira "it pays for itself. literally.">>

She sits at her desk, spinning slightly.

<<kira "you stream today?">>

<<eli "yeah. same numbers.">>

<<kira "consistency’s not bad.">>

<<eli "doesn’t feel good either.">>

She shrugs lightly.

<<kira "feelings are optional. metrics aren’t.">>

A small pause.

<<eli "i should head before i drip everywhere.">>

<<kira "yeah, go home and change. text me when you’re not a puddle.">>

<<eli "will do. bye.">>

[[Leave|neighbourhood]]

:: chat_kira_norm_2

The rain is lighter this time, but Eli’s still damp when Kira opens the door, already holding a mug.

<<kira "welcome back, rain magnet.">>

<<eli "i swear it wasn’t raining earlier.">>

<<kira "it sensed you.">>

I step in, shoes squeaking faintly. The apartment smells like green tea and something sweet.

<<eli "that smells good.">>

<<kira "tea. want some?">>

<<eli "sure.">>

She hands him a mug without ceremony.

<<kira "careful, it’s hot.">>

<<eli "thanks.">>

I take a sip, shoulders relaxing slightly. warm… didn’t realize how cold i was.

<<kira "you look less dead today.">>

<<eli "that’s progress.">>

<<kira "low bar, but we take it.">>

She leans against the desk.

<<kira "what’d you stream?">>

<<eli "same game.">>

<<kira "you ever get bored of it?">>

<<eli "yeah. but switching feels worse.">>

Kira nods knowingly.

<<kira "audience inertia. annoying but real.">>

A beat.

<<eli "i’ll head before i finish all your tea.">>

<<kira "you barely drank any. but okay. later, eli.">>

<<eli "later.">>

[[Leave|neighbourhood]]

:: chat_kira_norm_3

Thunder rumbles faintly outside as I knocks. Kira opens quickly this time, eyebrows raised.

<<kira "okay, wow you’re really wet. welcome.">>

<<eli "it got worse.">>

Water drips from my sleeves onto the floor.

<<kira "hold on stay there.">>

She disappears and comes back with a larger towel.

<<kira "here. emergency protocol.">>

<<eli "you have protocols?">>

<<kira "for you? yeah.">>

I dries off awkwardly. The room smells like fabric softener and faint perfume.

<<eli "sorry. didn’t mean to show up like this.">>

<<kira "you always show up like this. it’s your brand now.">>

I look exhausted… more than usual.

<<kira "you okay?">>

<<eli "just tired. streamed longer than usual.">>

<<kira "any payoff?">>

<<eli "not really.">>

She hums softly.

<<kira "it stacks eventually. just… slow.">>

<<eli "yeah.">>

A quiet moment.

<<eli "i should go before i flood your place.">>

<<kira "yeah, go dry off properly. later.">>

<<eli "bye.">>

