:: chat_kira_rom_1

Rain falls in a soft, steady curtain outside as I reaches Kira’s door, hoodie damp but not soaked. When she opens it, she pauses for half a second longer than usual, eyes scanning him.

<<kira "…wow. you’re actually not drenched. welcome.">>

<<eli "i’m improving. slowly.">>

I step in. The apartment smells like vanilla and fresh coffee, warm and grounding. Kira lingers near the door a moment, arms loosely crossed, a faint smile tugging at her lips. I looks… different today. lighter. it suits him.

<<kira "you look less miserable. should i be concerned?">>

<<eli "maybe it’s a phase.">>

<<kira "shame. i was starting to like it.">>

I lets out a quiet huff of a laugh, setting my bag down.

<<eli "harsh.">>

<<kira "honest.">>

She moves back toward her desk but slower than usual, glancing at him again.

<<kira "how’d stream go?">>

<<eli "hit twenty again… for a bit.">>

<<kira "again? okay, that’s not luck anymore.">>

I doesn’t even realize how big that is to him yet.

<<eli "it didn’t stick though.">>

<<kira "it doesn’t have to yet. it’s movement.">>

A quiet settles but not awkward. Just… full. Kira leans against the edge of her desk, tilting her head.

<<kira "come here for a second.">>

<<eli "what?">>

<<kira "just come here.">>

I hesitates, then steps closer. She reaches up, brushing a damp strand of hair off my forehead with surprising gentleness.

<<kira "you always show up looking like this.">>

I freezes slightly. what is this…

<<eli "like what?">>

<<kira "like you ran through a storm to get here.">>

Her hand lingers a second too long before dropping. A beat.

<<eli "i… should go.">>

<<kira "yeah. before i start charging you for floor damage.">>

I nods, stepping back.

<<eli "later.">>

<<kira "later, eli.">>

[[Leave|neighbourhood]]


